  "details": "Persistent in VRC. Imagine a game with a leaderboard showing top scores and hours played, all connected to an API. This could allow creators to have their own website where players can check their scores, hours, and more. For example, on the website, players could view their character, achievements, collections, etc., similar to how it works in WoW.\n\nIt could also connect to:\n\n- App\n\n- Website\n\n- Discord Bot\n\n- [String Loading](https://creators.vrchat.com/worlds/udon/string-loading/)\n\nAPI Usage\n\nBut before publish to the world, Creator can have options to checked on for API and Auto Generator Key next to \"World Debugging\" buttons when they need it.\n\nGenerator Key: How to assign unique keys for world IDs.\n\nData Display: Instructions on showing scores, achievements, or stats within a VRChat world and external platforms.\n\nTo make it easier for creators, the API Persistent system. It could include steps for generating unique keys per world ID, so creators can easily integrate it into their projects.",
